  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_CHRONICLE', origin: :published)
    ---
    
    *Nailed to the junction-post at Fourth Descent, Tunnel ☽'umbraor. Courier ink on cured seal-hide, stamped twice with the owl-and-fire-core seal of The Cell. The ink bleeds slightly in the damp; the hide smells of fire-core oil and old brine. Three of five seal-impressions are legible.*
    
    ---
    
    ## ☽ WANTED — ROUTE-SILENCE BROKEN — REWARD STANDS ☽
    ### By Authority of The Cell (owl-sworn), Under Pactum∴silenti
    
    ---
    
    **SUBJECT:** GLOW-TRADER VAULIUS-PHANTASM~. Known associate of Void-Merchant Valveus-morb~ (sought separately; whereabouts material). Medium build; charcoal wraps layered heavier than trade warrants. Fire-core amulet worn at the throat — touching it constantly; fingers that twitch near fire-cores even in still air. Courier ink stains on both flippers; origin of trade-name unverified and under formal challenge. Speaks in closed proverbs — circles his meaning the way a current circles a drain. Last confirmed: lower market stalls, sub-third descent, within sight of the Fissure's cold pulse. Absent from regular trade-posts for days following aurora activity. *The tunnel that hides you also traps you.*
    
    ---
    
    **OFFENSES, VERIFIED BY OATH AND SEAL:**
    
    Route betrayal under Pactum∴silenti; unauthorized diversion of Drift-coalesce glacial passages to unregistered buyers. Sale of aurora-crystals carrying the light no fire-core produces — cargo pulled from below surveyed depth, post-desecration, where no authorized trade-route exists. Unsanctioned contact with entities and sources at the Glow-Fissure since the drowning; extraction of material from sanctified ground now under Fire Keeper jurisdiction. Broken silence regarding ☽'☽'numu' Witness transit knowledge. Commerce in what seeps through where the veil will not close. *What the ice witnessed, the ice remembers.*
    
    ---
    
    **REWARD:** Twelve fire-cores, uncut, from Cell reserves. Report sightings to any tunnel bearing the owl-seal below fourth depth; speak the phrase *"the current returns."* Valveus-morb~ delivered alongside merits an additional four cores. The Cell honors its debts. *We remember every one.*
    
    ---
    
    **CAUTION:** Do not approach. Do not accept trade. Do not look at what he carries when the light shifts cold and blue-green. He has been too deep; he has been too long near what listens. The frozen sea is the only wall he needs. Report and withdraw.
    
    ---
    
    *Authenticated: ☽'etuseius, Keeper of Tolls, on behalf of what remains and what endures.*
    
    *☽ THE CELL STANDS ☽*
  CANONICAL_CHRONICLE
  annotation "note_1771585388984_0", anchor: "Absent from regular trade-posts for days following aurora activity", text: "He vanishes when the aurora peaks. He trades in 'what seeps through where the veil will not close.' Read these together. The Glow-Fissure is a breach-point; aurora activity thins the boundary between the living world and what lies beneath it. Vaulius-phantasm~ times his extractions to periods of maximum permeability. The Cell frames this as route betrayal. It is not. It is harvesting from a wound that opens on a schedule — and the Cell knows the schedule because they once built trade routes around it.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771585388984_1", anchor: "on behalf of what remains and what endures", text: "Every other Cell authentication in my archive reads 'what is held and what is owed' — creditor's language, proprietary, confident. This is different. 'What remains and what endures' is an institution counting what it has left.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771585388984_2", anchor: "he has been too long near what listens", text: "Not what watches. What listens. Deep-tunnel operational reports use this construction exclusively for presences that predate penguin habitation of the Berg. The Cell is not warning you about a fugitive merchant. They are warning you about what has noticed him.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
